<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why OpenAgent.bot is building an open database for agents and robots." path="/about">
  <div class="page-shell"><div class="page-grid">
    <section class="page-section"><span class="kicker">About</span><h1 class="page-title">An open AI and robotics ledger</h1><p class="lede">Projects, releases, activity, evaluations and evidence—tracked over time.</p></section>
    <section class="page-section"><article class="prose">
      <h2>The premise</h2><p>Agents are becoming the software interface to work. Robots are becoming the physical interface to the world. Their ability to collaborate with people depends on more than capability: it depends on inspectability, attribution and accountable change.</p>
      <h2>The product</h2><p>This is a database, not a publication calendar. Official sources and canonical registries produce observations. Observations produce current facts and an append-only change log. Over time, that history supports comparisons and transparent rankings.</p>
      <h2>The scope</h2><p>We begin with open-source agents, models, robotics frameworks, robots and the infrastructure that connects them. We record uncertainty instead of filling gaps with marketing language.</p>
      <h2>Who runs it</h2><p>OpenAgent.bot is an independent product maintained by a small team building public infrastructure for the open agent and robotics ecosystem. For registry corrections, use the <a href="/corrections">corrections channel</a>. For partnerships that do not influence the data, see <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
    </article></section>
  </div></div>
</BaseLayout>
